                <pb facs="0487" n="391" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg391"/>

                <head>No. 206.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wing to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Quito,
                                Ecuador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 2, 1873</date>.
                        (Received December 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 347.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Since the reception of dispatch No. 126
                    from the Department, I have had an interview with Minister Leon, who stated to
                    me that thus far all efforts to discover the perpetrators of the outrage upon
                    the Protestant cemetery near this city had proved unavailing.</p>
                <p>He added that the search was still being prosecuted, and promised that the
                    severest penalties would be inflicted upon the miscreants, in case of their
                    eventual capture.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>RUMSEY WING.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
